 10 seconds`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Claude Code picks the command’s working directory by `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#where-the-helper-runs`,children:`where you configured the server`}),`, so give the script as an absolute path or put it on `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`PATH`})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Dynamic headers override any static `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`headers`}),` with the same name`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Claude Code runs the helper fresh on each connection, at session start and on reconnect, once the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#trust-a-folder-before-its-headershelper-runs`,children:`trust rule for project and local-scope servers`}),` lets it run. It doesn’t cache the result, so your script is responsible for any token reuse.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`If a tool call returns `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`401 Unauthorized`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`403 Forbidden`}),`, Claude Code automatically re-runs the helper under the same rule, reconnects with the fresh headers, and retries the call once. Claude Code marks the server as needing authentication in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/mcp`}),` only if that retry also fails.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Claude Code sets these environment variables when executing the helper:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(Table,{children:[_jsx(_components.thead,{children:_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Variable`}),_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Value`})]})}),_jsxs(_components.tbody,{children:[_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`CLAUDE_CODE_MCP_SERVER_NAME`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`the name of the MCP server`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`CLAUDE_CODE_MCP_SERVER_URL`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`the URL of the MCP server`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`the plugin’s root directory. Set only when a `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/plugins-reference#mcp-servers`,children:`plugin`}),` provides the server`]})]})]})]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Use these to write a single helper script that serves multiple MCP servers.`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`A plugin-provided `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`headersHelper`}),` can’t reference the plugin’s `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/plugins-reference#user-configuration`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:\"${user_config.*}\"})}),` values, because the command runs through a shell. Claude Code reports the server as misconfigured with an `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/errors#plugin-command-references-user-config`,children:`error`}),` and doesn’t substitute the value. Put `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:\"${user_config.KEY}\"}),` in the server’s `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`headers`}),` field instead, which isn’t shell-parsed, or have the helper script read the value from a config file. Before v2.1.207, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`headersHelper`}),` substituted `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:\"${user_config.*}\"}),` values.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`4`,id:`where-the-helper-runs`,children:`Where the helper runs`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Claude Code picks the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`headersHelper`}),` command’s working directory from the configuration that declares the server. A `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`cd`}),` later in the session doesn’t move it. Each row below gives the directory that a relative path in your `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`headersHelper`}),` command resolves against.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(Table,{children:[_jsx(_components.thead,{children:_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Where you configured the server`}),_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Working directory`})]})}),_jsxs(_components.tbody,{children:[_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`A `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/plugins-reference#mcp-servers`,children:`plugin`})]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`The plugin’s root directory. Requires Claude Code v2.1.195 or later`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`A project `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.mcp.json`}),`, a `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#local-scope`,children:`local-scope`}),` server, an agent file in your project, a server from the SDK’s `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mcpServers`}),` option or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`setMcpServers()`}),` method, or `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/cli-reference`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--mcp-config`})})]}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`The directory you started Claude Code in`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#user-scope`,children:`User scope`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/managed-mcp`,children:`managed MCP`}),`, a `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#use-mcp-servers-from-claude-ai`,children:`claude.ai connector`}),`, or an agent file from outside your project, including one from an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--add-dir`}),` directory`]}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`Your configuration directory, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`~/.claude`}),` unless you set `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/env-vars`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`})})]})]})]})]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Before v2.1.238, Claude Code also ran the helpers of user-scope, managed, and claude.ai connector servers, and of agent files from outside your project, from the directory you started it in.`}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`4`,id:`which-variables-a-helper-can-read`,children:`Which variables a helper can read`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`A `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`headersHelper`}),` that a repository or plugin supplies is a command you didn’t write, so Claude Code runs it without the credential variables from your environment, such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`}),`. Where you configured the server decides whether this applies:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Removed`}),`: a server in a project `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.mcp.json`}),` or in a plugin, and an inline server in an agent file from your project or from an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--add-dir`}),` directory`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Not removed`}),`: a server at `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#user-scope`,children:`user`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#local-scope`,children:`local scope`}),`, in `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/managed-mcp`,children:`managed MCP`}),`, from a `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#use-mcp-servers-from-claude-ai`,children:`claude.ai connector`}),`, or supplied by the SDK or `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/cli-reference`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--mcp-config`})}),`, and an inline server in an agent file from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`~/.claude/agents/`}),`, from managed settings, or passed with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--agents`})]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Apart from Git’s `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_\u003cn\u003e`}),` variables, Claude Code removes every variable from your environment whose name has `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`TOKEN`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`SECRET`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`PASSWORD`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`PASSWD`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`PASSPHRASE`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`KEY`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`AUTH`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`COOKIE`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`PAT`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`DSN`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`CREDENTIAL`}),`, or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`CREDENTIALS`}),` as one of its underscore-separated parts, in either letter case, such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`MY_REGISTRY_TOKEN`}),`. Claude Code also removes a fixed list of credential variables whose names don’t follow that pattern, such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS`}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`When this applies to your helper, have the script read its credential from a file or a credential store. If the server’s `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`url`}),` `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#environment-variable-expansion-in-mcp-json`,children:`expands one of these variables`}),`, the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`CLAUDE_CODE_MCP_SERVER_URL`}),` value the helper receives has that part replaced with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`REDACTED`}),` as well.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`4`,id:`trust-a-folder-before-its-headershelper-runs`,children:`Trust a folder before its headersHelper runs`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Claude Code executes a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`headersHelper`}),` as an arbitrary shell command. For a server in a project `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.mcp.json`}),` or at `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#local-scope`,children:`local scope`}),`, it runs the helper only after you accept the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/permissions#project-allow-rules-and-workspace-trust`,children:`trust dialog`}),` for the folder you started the session in. Before v2.1.238, a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude -p`}),` or SDK session ran these helpers without checking trust, and an interactive session ran them once you had trusted a parent folder.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Trust that doesn’t count`}),`: a parent folder’s trust, and the automatic trust a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude -p`}),` or SDK session gets for `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/permissions#what-runs-before-you-trust-a-folder`,children:`hooks in settings files`})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Until you trust the folder`}),`: Claude Code connects the server with its static `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`headers`}),` alone. In a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude -p`}),` or SDK session it also prints one `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/errors#headershelper-not-run`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`headersHelper not run`})}),` line per server to stderr, telling you how to grant the trust.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Trust without a dialog`}),`: set `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`projects[\"\u003cpath\u003e\"].hasTrustDialogAccepted`}),` to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`}),` in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`~/.claude.json`}),`. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\u003cpath\u003e`}),` is the folder `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/permissions#project-allow-rules-and-workspace-trust`,children:`Project allow rules and workspace trust`}),` says Claude Code keys the trust on.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Claude Code applies the same rule to a server declared inline in an `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/sub-agents#scope-mcp-servers-to-a-subagent`,children:`agent file`}),`, checking where that agent file came from: your project, for a file in its `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/agents/`}),` directory, or an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--add-dir`}),` directory. Until you `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/permissions#what-runs-before-you-trust-a-folder`,children:`trust that project or directory itself`}),`, Claude Code doesn’t load the server at all, so its helper never runs either.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`add-mcp-servers-from-json-configuration`,children:`Add MCP servers from JSON configuration`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`If you have a JSON configuration for an MCP server, you can add it directly:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(Steps,{children:[_jsx(Step,{title:`Add an MCP server from JSON`,children:_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`11`,language:`shellscript`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`shellscript`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`shellscript`,numberOfLines:`11`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#6E7781`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#6A9955`},children:`# Basic syntax`})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#953800`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#DCDCAA`},children:`claude`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:` mcp`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:` add-json`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#CF222E`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:` \u003c`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:`nam`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`e`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#CF222E`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`\u003e`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"