he JSON must conform to the MCP server configuration schema`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`You can use `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--scope user`}),` to add the server to your user configuration instead of the project-specific one`]}),`\n`]})]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`import-mcp-servers-from-claude-desktop`,children:`Import MCP servers from Claude Desktop`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`If you’ve already configured MCP servers in Claude Desktop, you can import them:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(Steps,{children:[_jsx(Step,{title:`Import servers from Claude Desktop`,children:_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`2`,language:`shellscript`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`shellscript`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`shellscript`,numberOfLines:`2`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#6E7781`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#6A9955`},children:`# Basic syntax`})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#953800`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#DCDCAA`},children:`claude`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:` mcp`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:` add-from-claude-desktop`})]}),`\n`]})})})}),_jsx(Step,{title:`Select which servers to import`,children:_jsx(_components.p,{children:`After running the command, you’ll see an interactive dialog that allows you to select which servers you want to import.`})}),_jsx(Step,{title:`Verify the servers were imported`,children:_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`1`,language:`shellscript`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`shellscript`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`shellscript`,numberOfLines:`1`,children:[_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#953800`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#DCDCAA`},children:`claude`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:` mcp`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:` list`})]}),`\n`]})})})})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Server names added through `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude mcp`}),` commands can contain only letters, numbers, hyphens, and underscores. Claude Desktop doesn’t apply that restriction, so a Claude Desktop server whose name contains any other character, such as a space, can’t be imported. The import reports each name it rejects and still imports the other servers you selected. Before v2.1.205, the first invalid name stopped the import and none of the selected servers were added.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(Tip,{children:[_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Tips:`}),_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`This feature only works on macOS and Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL)`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`It reads the Claude Desktop configuration file from its standard location on those platforms`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Use the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--scope user`}),` flag to add servers to your user configuration`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`Imported servers keep the same names as in Claude Desktop when the name contains only letters, numbers, hyphens, and underscores. Claude Code reports a server whose name contains any other character and skips it`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`If servers with the same names already exist, they get a numerical suffix (for example, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`server_1`}),`)`]}),`\n`]})]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`use-mcp-servers-from-claude-ai`,children:`Use MCP servers from claude.ai`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`If you’ve logged into Claude Code with a `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://claude.ai`,children:`claude.ai`}),` account, MCP servers you’ve added in claude.ai, known as `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://claude.com/docs/connectors`,children:`connectors`}),`, are automatically available in Claude Code:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(Steps,{children:[_jsx(Step,{title:`Configure MCP servers in claude.ai`,children:_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Add servers at `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://claude.ai/customize/connectors`,children:`claude.ai/customize/connectors`}),`. On Team and Enterprise plans, only admins can add servers.`]})}),_jsx(Step,{title:`Authenticate the MCP server`,children:_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Complete any required authentication steps in claude.ai.`})}),_jsxs(Step,{title:`View and manage servers in Claude Code`,children:[_jsx(_components.p,{children:`In Claude Code, use the command:`}),_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,wrap:`true`,numberOfLines:`2`,language:`text`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`text`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`text`,numberOfLines:`2`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{children:`/mcp`})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{})})]})})}),_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Servers from claude.ai appear in the list with indicators showing they come from claude.ai.`})]})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Connectors you have never signed in to are collapsed behind a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Show unused connectors`}),` row at the end of the claude.ai section, so an organization-provisioned list doesn’t fill the panel. Select the row to expand them. A connector you signed in to before stays visible even when it currently needs re-authentication.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Connectors from claude.ai are fetched only when your active `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/authentication#authentication-precedence`,children:`authentication method`}),` is a claude.ai subscription login. They aren’t loaded, even if you previously ran `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/login`}),`, when:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`}),`, or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`apiKeyHelper`}),` is active`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`A third-party provider such as Amazon Bedrock or Google Cloud’s Agent Platform is active`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ANTHROPIC_PROFILE`}),`, the federation variables, or an active `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/authentication#anthropic-profiles-and-federation-credentials`,children:`Anthropic profile`}),` supplies the credential`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`}),` holds a token from `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/authentication#generate-a-long-lived-token`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude setup-token`})}),`, which can only make model requests`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`If `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/mcp`}),` doesn’t list a connector you added, run `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/status`}),` to confirm which authentication method is active. Unset that environment variable, remove the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`apiKeyHelper`}),` setting, or `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/authentication#anthropic-profiles-and-federation-credentials`,children:`switch off the profile`}),`, then run `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/login`}),` to select your claude.ai account.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`If `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/mcp`}),` shows a connector as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`connected · session token rejected`}),`, or its detail view shows `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/errors#claude-ai-rejected-the-session-token`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`claude.ai rejected the session token`})}),`, claude.ai rejected the token from your Claude Code login, usually because the login expired and couldn’t be refreshed. Authorizing the connector again doesn’t clear this state, because the connector’s own authorization in claude.ai isn’t what was rejected. To clear it:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ol,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Run `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/login`}),` to sign in again.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Reconnect the connector from `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/mcp`}),`.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Before v2.1.222, Claude Code marked connectors as needing authentication instead, and authorizing them didn’t resolve it.`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`A server you’ve added in Claude Code takes `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#scope-hierarchy-and-precedence`,children:`precedence`}),` over a claude.ai connector that points at the same URL. When this happens, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/mcp`}),` lists the connector as hidden and shows how to remove the duplicate if you’d rather use the connector.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Some Anthropic-hosted connectors, such as Microsoft 365, Gmail, and Google Calendar, don’t support local OAuth from Claude Code because the upstream identity provider only accepts the redirect URL that claude.ai registered. Authenticating one of these hosts in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/mcp`}),` shows a message directing you to connect it at Settings → Connectors on claude.ai instead. Once connected there, the connector appears in Claude Code automatically.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`organization-controls-on-connector-tools`,children:`Organization controls on connector tools`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Your organization can set per-tool controls on `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://claude.com/docs/connectors`,children:`claude.ai connectors`}),`. Claude Code reads these settings at startup and enforces them locally. Run `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/mcp`}),` to see which setting applies to each tool on a connector.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsxs(_components.strong,{children:[`Tool set to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ask`})]}),`: Claude Code prompts on every call with the reason `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Your organization requires approval for this tool`}),`. The prompt appears even in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`acceptEdits`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`auto`}),`, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`bypassPermissions`}),` `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/permissions#permission-modes`,children:`permission modes`}),`, and never offers an option to remember your choice. `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/permissions`,children:`Allow rules`}),` that match the tool don’t skip the prompt either. In `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`dontAsk`}),` mode, which never prompts, Claude Code denies the call instead.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsxs(_components.strong,{children:[`Tool set to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`blocked`})]}),`: Claude Code filters the tool out before Claude sees it, so it never appears in the tool list.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`disable-claude-ai-connectors`,children:`Disable claude.ai connectors`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`To disable claude.ai MCP servers in Claude Code, set `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/settings-reference#disableclaudeaiconnectors`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`disableClaudeAiConnectors`})}),` to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`}),` in any settings scope:`]}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`3`,language:`json`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`json`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`json`,numberOfLines:`3`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`{`})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#116329`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#9CDCFE`},children:`  \"disableClaudeAiConnectors\"`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`: `}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0550AE`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#569CD6`},children:`true`})]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`}`})}),`\n`]})})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`This setting uses any-source-true semantics: `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`}),` in any settings source takes precedence. A checked-in project `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/settings.json`}),` can opt a repository out of cloud connectors, but a project-level `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`false`}),` can’t re-enable connectors that a user- or policy-level `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`true`}),` has disabled. Servers passed explicitly via `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--mcp-config`}),` are unaffected.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`You can also set the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ENABLE_CLAUDEAI_MCP_SERVERS`}),` environment variable to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`false`}),`, which has the same effect for the current shell session:`]}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`1`,language:`shellscript`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`shellscript`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`shellscript`,numberOfLines:`1`,children:[_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#9CDCFE`},children:`ENABLE_CLAUDEAI_MCP_SERVERS`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#CF222E`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`=`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:`false`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#953800`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#DCDCAA`},children:` claude`})]}),`\n`]})})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`To block individual claude.ai connectors instead of all of them, add them to `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/managed-mcp`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deniedMcpServers`})}),` by name or by URL pattern. For example, a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`serverName`}),` entry of `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"claude.ai Slack\"`}),` blocks the Slack connector. To toggle a connector on or off for the current project only, use the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/mcp`}),` panel.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Note,{children:_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`These client-side settings govern local Claude Code sessions. In `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/claude-code-on-the-web`,children:`Claude Code on the web`}),` sessions, claude.ai connectors are provisioned by the remote host and arrive as explicit `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--mcp-config`}),` entries, so `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`disableClaudeAiConnectors`}),` doesn’t apply there. Connector URLs are also rewritten through the session proxy, so a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`deniedMcpServers`}),` `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`serverUrl`}),` pattern targeting the vendor URL won’t match. Manage which connectors a cloud session can use from your claude.ai organization settings.`]})}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`use-claude-code-as-an-mcp-server`,children:`Use Claude Code as an MCP server`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`You can use Claude Code itself as an MCP server that other applications can connect to:`}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`2`,language:`shellscript`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`shellscript`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`shellscript`,numberOfLines:`2`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#6E7781`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#6A9955`},children:`# Start Claude as a stdio MCP server`})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#953800`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#DCDCAA`},children:`claude`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:` mcp`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:` serve`})]}),`\n`]})})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`The command prints nothing when it starts. A stdio MCP server communicates over stdin and stdout, so a silent, blocked terminal means the server is running and waiting for a client to connect.`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`You can use this in Claude Desktop by adding this configuration to claude_desktop_config.json:`}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`10`,language:`json`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`json`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`json`,numberOfLines:`10`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`